          carries both letter pages, the breakdown bar and every swatch.
SUMMARY   Two bugs, both reported by Shade from a print of the live site.
          (1) Below 1024px the X-Ray collapsed to one column with the letter
          under the entire findings list, so selecting a row scrolled a pane
          that was off-screen — it looked like nothing happened. Now the
          letter is pinned to the top on narrow screens and the list scrolls
          beneath it. Needed flex, not grid: a sticky grid item can only stick
          inside its own cell, which in one column is exactly its own height.
          (2) Printing: the viewer's 78vh scroll box clipped the letter to one
          page, and the print-time relayout fired the width observer, which
          cleared each canvas and redrew it asynchronously while the browser
          took its snapshot — so the letter printed blank or not at all.
          Background colors were also dropped, erasing the aid bar and swatches
          (icons and labels survived, so nothing became ambiguous).
